  "strategy": "Approach and rationale: The central idea is to use a gradient-based optimization with multiple restarts and resolution levels to minimize the maximum overlap. Unlike previous approaches, we implement dimensionality reduction by using a coarser representation with interpolation, allowing the optimization to handle higher resolutions efficiently. We also introduce adaptive gradient steps and randomized projections to escape local optima. While this may not guarantee a global optimum, it offers better exploration than prior methods.\n\nMathematical specification: We represent h(x) as a grid function with n points. The objective is:\n   C5 = max_k \u222b[0,2] h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\nWe approximate this using FFT cross-correlation with binning. The constraints are:\n   \u2211 h_i * dx = 1\n  0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1 for all i\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Set up scales [32, 64, 128, 256, 512] for progressive optimization\n2. For each scale:\n   a. Upsample from coarse parents if available\n   b. Initialize with Thue-Morse sequence if parent is None\n   c. Perform gradient descent with momentum\n   d. Advancement criteria: decrease max correlation by 1% or hit target threshold\n3. After scale-up, interpolate and re-verify\n4. Use global random restarts with directed mutations\n5. Project candidate solutions to [0,1] and sum=1\n6. Compute score via FFT correlation only for valid solutions\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Scales: [32,64,128,256,512] (low to high resolution)\n- Momentum factor: 0.9\n- Step size: 0.6 (initial), adaptive later\n- Max iterations: 500,000 per restart\n- Random seeds from 0-1000 for restarts\n- Target: 0.3808\n- Fallback parent: Thue-Morse interpolation\n\nNumerical robustness and memory use:\n- Track valid candidates after each scale-up\n- Clip values to [0,1] post-update\n- Handle FFT correlation with dx=2/n_points\n- Maintain sum by clamping min/max\n\nRuntime safeguards and return contract:\n- Break iterations if time budget exhausted\n- Skip scales if memory exceeds limits\n- Return closest valid candidate via projection if timer fails\n- Compute score with exact correlation if FFT unavailable",
